From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:39:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btmt6797: don't ask for the MWS transport
 configuration

The controller lists Get MWS Transport Layer Configuration among its supported
commands, then refuses it with status 0x02, which fails the core's init. Gemian's
3.18 core drops this command for the same reason, with a comment that the chip
misbehaves. Nothing uses MWS here.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c
index 68bf9e201..3559f4f95 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c
@@ -211,6 +211,7 @@ static int btmt6797_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	hdev->set_bdaddr = btmt6797_set_bdaddr;
 	hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_NON_PERSISTENT_SETUP);
 	hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_RESET_ON_CLOSE);
+	hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_MWS_TRANSPORT_CONFIG);
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, bt);
 	ret = hci_register_dev(hdev);
 	if (ret < 0)
-- 
2.43.0

